---
import { getCollection, render } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import TierTag from '../components/TierTag.astro';
import Annotation from '../components/Annotation.astro';
import PrincipleRefs from '../components/PrincipleRefs.astro';
import { t, localePath } from '../lib/i18n.js';

const locale = 'en';

const all = await getCollection('goodUses', (entry) => entry.id.startsWith('en/'));

const entries = await Promise.all(
  all
    .sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order)
    .map(async (entry) => {
      const { Content } = await render(entry);
      return { slug: entry.id.split('/').slice(1).join('/'), data: entry.data, Content };
    })
);

const providers = entries.filter((e) => e.data.audience === 'provider');
const intermediaries = entries.filter((e) => e.data.audience === 'intermediary');

const groups = [
  {
    id: 'for-providers',
    heading: 'For providers',
    intro:
      'Eight places where the work is real, the risk is manageable and the time comes back to the floor.',
    items: providers,
  },
  {
    id: 'for-intermediaries',
    heading: 'For the nonprofits and intermediaries that support them',
    intro:
      'Four places where a resource and referral agency, a coaching network or a lender can reach more providers with the staff it already has.',
    items: intermediaries,
  },
];

const description =
  'Twelve constructive uses of AI in early childhood, each with its risk tier and its guardrail: the unglamorous, low-risk work that returns hours to a program running on thin margins.';
---

<BaseLayout title="Where AI helps" description={description} locale={locale}>
  <PageHeader
    caption="Where AI earns its place"
    title="Where AI helps"
    lede="Most of what AI can do in early childhood is unglamorous, low-risk and worth real money to a business running on 1–3% margins — and every hour it returns is an hour an adult spends with children."
    locale={locale}
  />

  <p class="govuk-body">
    A site that is only a list of prohibitions will be read once and never
    returned to. This page is the <a class="govuk-link" href={`${localePath(locale, '/principles')}#relationship`}>Relationship
    principle</a> made concrete, and it is also the page that makes the <a class="govuk-link" href={localePath(locale, '/bright-lines')}>bright
    lines</a> credible. A framework that only says no reads as hostile to a
    director who is drowning. A framework that says <em>here is where this
    genuinely helps, and here is the short list where it doesn't</em> reads as
    useful.
  </p>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Every entry below carries its risk tier and its guardrail, because the point
    is not that these uses are unregulated — it is that they are worth doing
    carefully.
  </p>

  <nav class="govuk-!-margin-bottom-8" aria-labelledby="contents-heading">
    <h2 class="govuk-heading-s" id="contents-heading">{t(locale, 'label.onThisPage')}</h2>
    {groups.map((group) => (
      <>
        <h3 class="govuk-heading-s govuk-!-margin-bottom-1">{group.heading}</h3>
        <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number govuk-!-margin-bottom-4">
          {group.items.map((item) => (
            <li>
              <a class="govuk-link" href={`#${item.slug}`}>{item.data.title}</a>{' '}
              <TierTag tier={item.data.tier} locale={locale} link={false} />
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </>
    ))}
  </nav>

  {groups.map((group) => (
    <section id={group.id}>
      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">{group.heading}</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">{group.intro}</p>

      {group.items.map((item) => {
        const Body = item.Content;
        return (
        <article id={item.slug} class="govuk-!-margin-bottom-9">
          <h3 class="govuk-heading-s govuk-!-margin-bottom-2">{item.data.title}</h3>
          <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-4">
            <TierTag tier={item.data.tier} locale={locale} withName={true} />
          </p>

          <p class="govuk-body-l">{item.data.scenario}</p>

          <div class="govuk-body">
            <Body />
          </div>

          <Annotation label={t(locale, 'label.returns')}>
            <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">{item.data.returns}</p>
          </Annotation>

          <Annotation label={t(locale, 'label.guardrail')}>
            <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">{item.data.guardrail}</p>
          </Annotation>

          <PrincipleRefs ids={item.data.governs} locale={locale} />
        </article>
        );
      })}
    </section>
  ))}

  <hr class="govuk-section-break govuk-section-break--visible govuk-!-margin-bottom-6" />

  <section id="the-rule-that-keeps-this-page-honest">
    <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">The rule that keeps this page honest</h2>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      Every entry on this page is missing its last line. On the live page, each
      one ends with what the program actually did with the time it got back —
      hired a floater, gave a teacher a paid planning hour, opened an infant
      slot, stopped working Sundays. Without that, this is an efficiency
      brochure, and the field has plenty of those. With it, it is the
      Relationship principle with receipts.
    </p>

    <div class="govuk-inset-text">
      <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">
        Those outcomes are not here yet. They have to be collected from real
        pilots rather than borrowed from vendor case studies, and that
        collection has not happened. This is a gap in the page, not a feature of
        it — and until it is filled, every claim above about returned hours is
        an argument rather than a result.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      Three things hold for every entry regardless: no product is named, the
      tier is stated, and the guardrail travels with the use.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
